<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Holiday returns three months after starting buprenorphine. Eight days ago, on tour in another state, the pharmacy could not refill her buprenorphine because the insurer&apos;s prior authorization had lapsed. After two days without it she had withdrawal and strong cravings, and six days ago she used heroin twice. She tested the supply first and the fentanyl strip was positive; she used with her friend present and naloxone at hand, and she did not overdose. The pharmacy filled the prescription the next day, and she restarted buprenorphine that morning, after waiting until she felt withdrawal again as she had been taught; she has taken it daily since and has used no opioids for five days. She also drank more on the tour, most nights. She called the clinic as soon as she was home and wanted to be seen. She is ashamed and worried that she has lost her place in treatment. She has had no thoughts of suicide. She feels tired and low and has not been sleeping well. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Return to use</td><td>Heroin twice, six days ago, after two days without buprenorphine</td></tr><tr><td>Cause of the gap</td><td>Lapsed prior authorization while on tour</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Tested the supply (fentanyl positive); used with her friend present and naloxone at hand; no overdose</td></tr><tr><td>Buprenorphine</td><td>Restarted five days ago at 16 mg daily, without precipitated withdrawal</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Drinking most nights on tour</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Tired, low, ashamed; PHQ-9 11; item 9 scored 0</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

